    "title": "Former YSU coach leads Utah State to March Madness win",
    "text": "Utah State head coach Jerrod Calhoun calls out to players during the first half of an NCAA college basketball game against UNLV in the quarterfinals of the Mountain West Conference tournament, Thursday, March 12, 2026, in Las Vegas, Nev … by: Liam Garrity Posted: Mar 20, 2026 / 06:48 PM EDT Updated: Mar 20, 2026 / 06:48 PM EDT EAST LIVERPOOL, Ohio (WKBN) – Former Youngstown State and current Utah State head coach Jerrod Calhoun led his squad to an 86-76 win over Villanova in the First Round of the NCAA Men’s Basketball Championship in San Diego, Friday afternoon. Calhoun coached the No. 9 Aggies over the No. 8 Wildcats in the First Round West Region victory. Aggie’s Mason Falslev scored a team-high 22 points in the win. Wildcat’s Bryce Lindsay recorded a game-high 25 points in the first-round loss. This is the third-straight NCAA Tournament appearance for the Aggies and the second consecutive time for Calhoun. In his two seasons at the helm, Calhoun has a record of 54-14. The East Liverpool native coached for seven seasons at YSU with a record of 118-106. Calhoun won the first regular-season conference championship in program history in 2022-23. Utah State advances to a season record of 29-6. Villanova’s season ends at 24-9. Next, No. 9 Utah State will face No. 1 Arizona on March 22 at an undecided time.",
